lan is merely long-winded, tighten the prose and move narration into ticket comments or a session log rather than fragmenting coherent work. Run `rebar explain plan` for the authoring guidance.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how an older binary's READ path behaves against a sharded/stamped store (the compat gate only blocks mutation), and confirm whether silent not-found from a flat-only resolver is acceptable or must itself be made to fail closed.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.435,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["compat.py docstring: 'refuses to mutate or externally publish a store ... while keeping reads and diagnostics available'","Step 6: 'The migration appends that token so older v1.0+ binaries fail closed while current binaries read the store' — but 'fail closed' applies to mutation, not reads","Step 10: 'before migration, readers handle both layouts ... after migration, all tickets resolve to shards' scopes only current-binary readers"],"finding":"The store-compat gate (compat.py) blocks only MUTATION/external-publish and keeps reads available, so an older binary can still READ a store stamped with 'sharded-ticket-layout' — but its flat-only _ids.py resolver will silently return 'ticket not found' for any sharded ticket instead of failing closed. The plan's expand-phase compatibility (step 10) only covers current binaries reading both layouts; it does not address how an old binary's read path degrades against a sharded store, so the compat token does not actually protect the read surface it implies.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcfcf037e80f71bec","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation Plan step 6 and step 10; compat gate contract in src/rebar/_store/compat.py","norm_id":"n6a66e749bbf4704b","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator migrates a store to sharded layout; an agent still on an older rebar binary runs `rebar show <sharded-id>` and gets a spurious not-found instead of a clear incompatibility error"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State why the shard is sha256(id)[:2] rather than the canonical id's own first two hex characters (e.g. even bucket distribution independent of id-generation structure).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4492,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope: 'Implement a fan-out layout tickets/<sha256-2>/<id>'","Step 1: 'sha256 first-2-hex shard/relpath derivation' — no stated rationale for sha256 over the id's own first-2-hex"],"finding":"The plan does not state a positive rationale for deriving the shard from sha256(id) rather than the simpler and reversible alternative of the first two hex characters of the canonical id itself. Both yield 256 buckets and the same churn reduction; the id is already 16-hex, so its own prefix is a natural shard key that needs no hashing and is inspectable/reversible without recomputation. The choice of sha256 is plausibly justified by even distribution (ids may not be uniformly distributed), but that rationale is absent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb997059daba34e37","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation Plan step 1 and Scope ('tickets/<sha256-2>/<id>')","norm_id":"ncd3a7ad6474e74e2","priority":0.1508,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or future maintainer cannot tell whether sha256 was chosen for distribution reasons or by habit, and may 'simplify' it to id-prefix and reintroduce skew"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"hard","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the fatal-collision abort and interrupted-resume states are surfaced to the operator (explicit error message/log line and non-zero exit or ensure failure status).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.884,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'refuses target collisions as fatal/permanent'","'If killed after renames but before commit, no partial commit exists; rerun completes the mixed working tree or an operator can reset it'","ABSENCE: no mention of a surfaced error message/log/exit status for the fatal-collision abort path"],"finding":"The migration's fatal collision and interrupted-resume failure modes are described as behaviors (abort, no-op, resume) but the plan does not state how these error/abort states are surfaced to the operator (log/message/exit signal), so an operator running the ensure could get a silent or opaque abort.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f12845dfd5f82e0a8","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation Plan step 5; AC: 'Migration collisions are fatal and atomic'","norm_id":"n67bd0b444672474b","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator runs the ensure-registry migration; two ids collide on the same shard target and the run aborts","Migration is killed mid-rename and the operator must decide whether to rerun or reset"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In step 5, add that a collision abort raises a distinct fatal error identifying the two source paths and target shard, and that rerun after an interrupted migration logs the mixed-state detection and completion, so the operator sees deterministic signals.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make explicit that after this change no consumer may join a resolver-returned id directly to the tracker root; every id-to-path build must go through the layout helper, and note how the inventory in step 4 is verified complete (e.g. a grep/selector for naked `os.path.join(tracker, id)`).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.3069,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_ids.py resolve_ticket_dir_name returns os.path.basename(name); docstring: 'Read sites that build a filesystem path from a ticket id use this'","Step 3: 'Keep resolver outputs separator-free. _ids.py returns ids/names only'","Step 4 enumerates a large consumer inventory that must all switch to the helper for path construction"],"finding":"The resolver contract change is under-specified for path construction. `resolve_ticket_id`/`resolve_ticket_dir_name` in _ids.py return a bare separator-free basename that today every read site joins directly as `os.path.join(tracker_dir, name)`. Under the shard layout a bare id no longer joins to a valid path (the ticket lives at `<tracker>/<shard>/<id>`). The plan keeps resolver outputs separator-free (step 3) and routes consumers through the layout helper (step 4), but does not state the now-load-bearing invariant that naked `os.path.join(tracker, id)` is forbidden — a single missed consumer resolves to a non-existent path and silently reads zero events rather than erroring.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4d9693cb5e4896f1","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation Plan steps 3-4; src/rebar/_ids.py resolve_ticket_id / resolve_ticket_dir_name","norm_id":"n725414a3ef380b78","priority":0.2931,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A consumer not in the step-4 inventory keeps doing os.path.join(tracker, resolved_id) and reads an empty/absent directory, returning 'no records' instead of the ticket's real state"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate"